    "intro_html":  "Chuletas guisadas is what happens when a Puerto Rican kitchen decides that a pork chop should never, ever be dry again. You sear the chops, then let them stew in a tomato and sofrito gravy with olives and peppers until they surrender. It is a completely different animal from a Southern smothered chop, which leans on cream and onion. This one is bright, acidic, and salty from the olives. It also happens to carry one of the highest protein numbers in this whole batch, which is not something you often say about comfort food.",
